# Proof of Delivery UI – Cursor Rule

## Objective

Build a pixel-perfect, accessible, and modern Proof of Delivery UI for the Parcego Courier workflow.  
**Focus:** Mobile-first, smooth UX for couriers to capture and upload delivery proof (photo, signature, notes, etc.), ready for future backend/API integration.

---

## 1. Technology & Design System

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com/)
- **State Management:** Zustand (if needed)
- **Transitions:** Use premium, subtle transitions as per `@premium-transitions-and-effects.mdc`
- **Accessibility:** All UI must be accessible (ARIA, keyboard navigation, color contrast)
- **Naming/Scoping:**  
  - All IDs and class names must strictly follow `@naming-and-scoping.mdc`:
    - IDs: `parcego-[component]-[purpose]-[unique-identifier]`
    - Classes: `parcego-[block]__[element]--[modifier]`
- **Icons:**  
  - All icons must use the kebab-case span structure (`iconify lucide-icon`), with `data-icon` attributes and inline styles.
  - Icon sizes must be visually balanced:  
    - Main actions: **24–32px**  
    - Status/secondary: **16–20px**
  - No direct Lucide React components in JSX.

---

## 2. Scope & Requirements

### Proof of Delivery UI Features (All UI, No Backend)
- **Photo Capture/Upload:**  
  - Prominent button to capture/upload photo (mobile camera or file picker).
  - Show photo preview with option to retake/remove.
- **GPS & Timestamp:**  
  - Display current location (mocked) and timestamp.
  - Use location/map icon (24px).
- **Digital Signature:**  
  - Canvas or input for courier/customer to sign.
  - Clear and Save buttons.
- **Notes/Comments:**  
  - Textarea for optional delivery notes.
- **Upload Button:**  
  - Large, visually distinct button to "Upload Proof" (with loading/feedback state).
- **Feedback & Confirmation:**  
  - Show success/failure feedback with premium transitions.
  - Option to return to dashboard or next delivery.
- **Navigation:**  
  - Back button (with icon, 20–24px).
- **Accessibility:**  
  - All elements must be keyboard accessible, have ARIA labels, and meet color contrast standards.
- **Responsiveness:**  
  - Mobile-first, fully responsive layout.
- **Transitions:**  
  - Use fade/slide-in for content, button feedback, and modal overlays.
- **Error Handling:**  
  - Show clear error messages for missing photo/signature, upload failure, etc.

---

## 3. UX Best Practices

- **Mobile-First:**  
  - Large touch targets, minimal input steps, clear feedback.
- **Instant Feedback:**  
  - Show loading spinners, success checkmarks, and error states.
- **Accessible:**  
  - ARIA labels, focus states, and keyboard navigation for all actions.
- **Visual Hierarchy:**  
  - Use card layouts, clear section headings, and spacing.
- **Premium Transitions:**  
  - Subtle, non-distracting animations for all interactive elements.
- **Consistent Icon Sizes:**  
  - Main actions: 28–32px; secondary/status: 16–20px.
- **Clear Call-to-Action:**  
  - Upload button is always visible and prominent.
- **Error Prevention:**  
  - Disable upload until all required fields are complete.

---

## 4. Code Quality & Structure

- Use TypeScript everywhere.
- Functional components only.
- Early returns, no dead code, no TODOs.
- Descriptive naming and clear structure.
- All forms, buttons, and flows must be visually complete and accessible.
- All IDs and class names must strictly follow `@naming-and-scoping.mdc`.
- All icons must follow the kebab-case span structure rule.

---

## 5. Deliverables

- Proof of Delivery page and all required UI components.
- Fully navigable UI demo (no backend).
- README update with instructions for running the demo.

---

## 6. Enforcement

- Code reviews must verify adherence to this rule file and referenced standards.
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by project lead.

